spec: S02-01, S02-02, S02-09, S02-10, S02-12, S02-13, S02-14, S17-03, S17-05, S17-08

push creates v1; the same bytes are a no-op; a change is v2; pushing v1's bytes again is v3
(same content as v1). Ticket 17: when the local Sidecar is behind, a file that lacks the head's
changes is refused (exit 5, the missing hunk shown) — a stale, unedited file too, `--strict` or
not — and `--discard-head-changes` is how a deliberate revert goes through. Merged stdout+stderr.

```console
$ annotary -p rowan push flow.md
flow	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan push flow.md
flow	[..]	already v1

$ annotary -p rowan push flow-v2/flow.md --doc flow -m "edit"
flow	[..]	v2

$ annotary -p rowan pull flow --out here
pull: 0 threads, 0 assets
flow.md	flow.annotary	v2

$ annotary -p rowan push here/flow.md
flow	[..]	already v2

$ annotary -p rowan push flow.md -m "back"
? 5
error: v2 by @rowan changed flow.md since your v1 — those changes are not in your file — put them into flow.md and push again
@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
 # Flow
 
-v1 text.
+v2 text.

$ annotary -p rowan push flow.md -m "back" --discard-head-changes
warning: discarding v2 by @rowan since your v1
flow	[..]	v3 (same content as v1)

$ annotary -p rowan push flow.md --json
{"name":"flow","id":"[..]","version":3,"same_as":1,"already":true}

$ annotary -p rowan versions flow --json number,same_as
[{"number":1},{"number":2},{"number":3,"same_as":1}]

$ annotary -p rowan pull flow --version 2 --force
pull: 0 threads, 0 assets
(name on v2 was "flow"; Threads as they were on v2; head is v3)
flow.md	flow.annotary	v2

$ annotary -p rowan push flow.md --strict
? 5
error: v3 by @rowan changed flow.md since your v2 — those changes are not in your file — put them into flow.md and push again
@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
 # Flow
 
-v2 text.
+v1 text.

$ annotary -p rowan push flow.md -m "again" --discard-head-changes
warning: discarding v3 by @rowan since your v2
flow	[..]	v4 (same content as v2)

$ annotary -p rowan push flow.md --json
{"name":"flow","id":"[..]","version":4,"same_as":2,"already":true}

```
